i9.py	TY for the error handling/use of the try except; and the handling of specific error conditions to produce specifc error messages - is nice. Great program with clear helper functions and specific helpful exception handling; using a set for uniqueness and random.sample for output is was my approach too, I did learn from your print(* and how that unpacks a container and hands each to the pring function.  Thank you! You're top of my set of PRs this week.  
2a.py	Clean, well-structured solution that correctly enforces letter-only words over 10 characters and uses random sampling of unique words; the handling of specific error conditions to produce specifc error messages - is nice. Interesting breaking logic into functions...sets up for object oriented coding; having a file object, that has a constructure that accepts a filepath, and you call it from this program, and it returns a file object and any exceptions it encountered..and every program you write that has to open a file. 
y6.py	Nice concise approach that lowercases, strips punctuation, filters correctly, and samples unique words, but adding argument/file error handling would make it more robust.  Really concise.  Impressed! Appreciated your commenting too. 
nt.py	No error handling for the file open and args.  Good use of set and random.sample with the right length check, but not removing punctuation means many valid long words are skipped when attacked to commas/periods, so it might not perform as you expect.  
35.py	You successfully build a unique list and sample random words, but missing punctuation cleanup and no try/except for file error handling, is a problem.  Need to include.
y7.py	Good effort with comments and exception handling, and the random unique output works, but not lowercase-ing can cause duplicate words "Lots of joy" and "Joy for lots" - each is a seperate unique word without lowercase-ing.
sc.py	You did a solid job reading and normalizing text, but this version misses key requirements because of no filter for words over 10 letters and does not actually pick random words (set.pop is not true random selection).